h bit; the number of ways to end with run length 1 is sum of both bits. Similarly for run length 2. So we can aggregate.\n\nLet A_n = total number of valid strings of length n ending with a run of length 1 (i.e., last bit different from previous). B_n = total number ending with run length 2.\n\nWe need initial: n=1: A_1 = 2 (both bits). B_1 = 0 (no run length 2 yet).\n\nTransition: To get A_{n+1}, we can add a bit that is different from previous bit. For any string of length n ending with run length 1 or 2, we can add opposite bit. So A_{n+1} = A_n + B_n (since from any state we can switch bit). To get B_{n+1}, we need to add same bit to a string ending with run length 1. So B_{n+1} = A_n (since only from run length 1 we can extend to run length 2). Because from run length 2 we cannot extend same"}}],"created":1790952980,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens":3713,"total_tokens":4481,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-XrBseGMFfF2XH301C7ZzBlKbQeK4Kob2","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":3713,"prompt_ms":446.672,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.12029948828440615,"prompt_per_second":8312.5873123903,"predicted_n":768,"predicted_ms":2356.342,"predicted_per_token_ms":3.0721538461538462,"predicted_per_second":325.50453202463814}}